        <h2>The grammar stays familiar. The language stays itself.</h2>
        <p>
          Python is the detailed example throughout this guide. TypeScript preserves the same
          architectural sentence with camelCase methods, asynchronous extraction, and native test
          matcher integration. Other ports adapt ownership, errors, parsing, and runners to their
          ecosystems rather than forcing a byte-for-byte translation.
        </p>
